From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 01:20:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 064/138] drm: adp: Add a draft driver for the Apple A8 (T7000)
 display pipe

First draft for the iPhone 6. It keeps everything iBoot set up (DSI,
panel, ADBE0 timings, the dart-disp0 page tables) and only programs the
pipe 0 base and stride, optionally latched with the parameter FIFO sync
word. Scanout buffers are allocated from the 12 MB vram carveout that
iBoot already maps in the display DART, after checking the mapping by
walking iBoot's tables, so no IOMMU hand-over is needed.

Vblank and flip completion use the ADP interrupt (AIC 103, enable
0x1028, W1C status 0x102c), with a storm guard. simpledrm is removed
through the aperture helpers after both power domains are held.

standalone=1 is a test mode that creates the device without a DT node
so the module can be loaded on a running kernel.

Untested on hardware.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
